    </custom_item>

    <custom_item>
      type        : CMD_EXEC
      description : "1.233 OL09-00-002080"
      info        : "OL 9 must prevent special devices on nonroot local partitions.

GROUP ID: V-271669
RULE ID: SV-271669r1184200

The \"nodev\" mount option causes the system to not interpret character or block special devices. Executing character or block special devices from untrusted file systems increases the opportunity for nonprivileged users to attain unauthorized administrative access.

The only legitimate location for device files is the \"/dev\" directory located on the root partition, with the exception of chroot jails if implemented."
      solution    : "Configure the \"/etc/fstab\" to use the \"nodev\" option on all nonroot local partitions."
      reference   : "800-171|3.4.2,800-171r3|03.04.02a.,800-53|CM-6b.,800-53r5|CM-6b.,CCI|CCI-000366,CN-L3|8.1.10.6(d),CSF|PR.IP-1,CSF2.0|DE.CM-09,CSF2.0|PR.PS-01,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ISO-27001-2022|A.8.9,ITSG-33|CM-6b.,LEVEL|2M,NESA|T3.2.1,Rule-ID|SV-271669r1184200_rule,STIG-ID|OL09-00-002080,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3,Vuln-ID|V-271669"
      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/27024"
      cmd         : "/bin/mount | /bin/grep -P '^/dev[\\S]* on /[\\S]+' | /bin/grep --invert-match 'nodev' | /bin/grep -E -v '\\bvfat\\b' | /bin/awk '{print} END {if (NR == 0) print \"nodev has been set appropriately for mounted /dev file systems\"; else print \"fail - nodev option not found on the following file systems\"}'"
      expect      : "^nodev has been set appropriately for mounted /dev file systems$"
    </custom_item>

