    <custom_item>
      type        : CMD_EXEC
      description : "1.398 OL09-00-003011"
      info        : "OL 9 must configure the use of the pam_faillock.so module in the /etc/pam.d/system-auth file.

GROUP ID: V-271837
RULE ID: SV-271837r1092223

If the pam_faillock.so module is not loaded, the system will not correctly lockout accounts to prevent password guessing attacks."
      solution    : "Configure OL 9 to include the use of the pam_faillock.so module in the /etc/pam.d/system-auth file.

Add/modify the appropriate sections of the \"/etc/pam.d/system-auth\" file to match the following lines:
Note: The \"preauth\" line must be listed before pam_unix.so.

auth required pam_faillock.so preauth
auth required pam_faillock.so authfail
account required pam_faillock.so"
      reference   : "800-171|3.1.8,800-171r3|03.01.08a.,800-53|AC-7a.,800-53r5|AC-7a.,CCI|CCI-000044,CN-L3|8.1.4.1(b),CSF2.0|PR.AA-03,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ISO-27001-2022|A.8.5,ITSG-33|AC-7a.,LEVEL|2A,NESA|T5.5.1,NIAv2|AM24,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|8.1.6,PCI-DSSv4.0|8.3.4,Rule-ID|SV-271837r1092223_rule,STIG-ID|OL09-00-003011,TBA-FIISB|45.1.2,TBA-FIISB|45.2.1,TBA-FIISB|45.2.2,Vuln-ID|V-271837"
      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/27024"
      cmd         : "/bin/awk '
        BEGIN{st=\"fail\";pu=0}
        /pam_unix.so/{pu=1}
        /^[\\s]*auth[^#\\n\\r]+pam_faillock\\.so[^#\\n\\r]+preauth/{print; if (pu==0){st=\"pass\"}}
        END{print st}' /etc/pam.d/system-auth"
      expect      : "^pass$"
    </custom_item>

    <custom_item>
      type        : CMD_EXEC
