    <custom_item>
      type        : FILE_CONTENT_CHECK
      description : "1.4 OL09-00-000004"
      info        : "OL 9 must use a separate file system for /tmp.

GROUP ID: V-271434
RULE ID: SV-271434r1091014

The \"/tmp\" partition is used as temporary storage by many programs. Placing \"/tmp\" in its own partition enables the setting of more restrictive mount options, which can help protect programs that use it."
      solution    : "Migrate the \"/tmp\" path onto a separate file system."
      reference   : "800-171|3.4.2,800-171r3|03.04.02a.,800-53|CM-6b.,800-53r5|CM-6b.,CCI|CCI-000366,CN-L3|8.1.10.6(d),CSF|PR.IP-1,CSF2.0|DE.CM-09,CSF2.0|PR.PS-01,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ISO-27001-2022|A.8.9,ITSG-33|CM-6b.,LEVEL|2A,NESA|T3.2.1,Rule-ID|SV-271434r1091014_rule,STIG-ID|OL09-00-000004,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3,Vuln-ID|V-271434"
      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/27024"
      file        : "/etc/fstab"
      regex       : "[\\s]+/tmp[\\s]+"
      expect      : "[\\s]+/tmp[\\s]+"
    </custom_item>

    <custom_item>
      type        : CMD_EXEC
      description : "1.40 OL09-00-000222"
